    ">\n",
    "> What's the difference between transform() and fit.transform()? - Answer Below\n",
    "\n",
    "The main difference between transform() and fit.transform() lies in the fact that transform doesn't calculate new statistics (mean and std) for the dataset it is applied on. This must be archieved though by using the fit() function separately beforehand. So fit_transform() does calculate mean and std beforehand and then transforms the datasets in such a fashion:\n",
    "\n",
    "$\n",
    "x_{trans}=\\frac{x-\\mu}{\\sigma}\n",
    "$\n",
    "\n",
    "It may be important to say that firstly, using the transform function without fitting before (calculating mean and std) seems useless, and secondly that fit() does NOT ALWAYS use mean / std (this only applies for the StandardScaler) \n"
   ]
